# ILIFA Website Enhancement Plan

## Important Instructions

Before making any changes:

1. Create a new feature branch.
2. Do NOT modify existing business logic unless specifically instructed.
3. Preserve all current functionality.
4. Implement changes incrementally.
5. After completing each phase:

   * Run the application.
   * Verify no existing pages are broken.
   * Check mobile responsiveness.
   * Check desktop responsiveness.
   * Commit changes before moving to the next phase.

---

# Phase 1: Landing Page Improvements

## Task 1: Fix Hero Section Layout

### Objective

Improve the positioning of the website title, tagline, and hero content to prevent overlap.

### Requirements

* Review current hero section layout.
* Ensure title, subtitle, and call-to-action buttons are properly aligned.
* Remove any overlapping elements.
* Maintain responsiveness across desktop, tablet, and mobile.

### Acceptance Criteria

* No overlapping text.
* Clean spacing between all hero elements.
* Responsive on all screen sizes.

---

## Task 2: Replace Static Hero Image with Video

### Objective

Improve user engagement by replacing the landing page hero image with a promotional video.

### Requirements

* Add support for a hero background video.
* Include a fallback image if video fails to load.
* Ensure video is optimized for performance.
* Add overlay to maintain text readability.

### Acceptance Criteria

* Video loads smoothly.
* Text remains readable.
* Mobile devices display correctly.

---

# Phase 2: Improve User Understanding

## Task 3: Add "What We Do" Section

### Objective

Clearly explain the purpose of ILIFA.

### Requirements

Create a section near the top of the landing page explaining:

* Property investment opportunities.
* Property purchasing process.
* Property development/building services.
* Benefits of using the platform.

### Acceptance Criteria

* New visitors understand the service within 30 seconds.
* Clear distinction between:

  * Buying property.
  * Building property.
  * Investing in property.

---

## Task 4: Clarify Property Services

### Objective

Reduce confusion around "Buy Property" and "Build Property".

### Requirements

Review wording throughout the website.

Possible improvements:

* Buy Property
* Build Your Home
* Property Development
* Investment Opportunities

Update labels only if clarity improves.

### Acceptance Criteria

* Users can easily understand the difference between services.

---

# Phase 3: User Onboarding

## Task 5: Create Onboarding Process Section

### Objective

Guide new users through the process.

### Requirements

Add a visual step-by-step onboarding section.

Suggested Flow:

Step 1:
Create an Account

Step 2:
Select Your Service

Step 3:
Choose a Package

Step 4:
Make Payment

Step 5:
Access Property Opportunities

Step 6:
Begin Your Investment Journey

### Acceptance Criteria

* Users can clearly see how to get started.
* Process is visible on homepage and onboarding pages.

---

## Task 6: Display Payment Packages

### Objective

Clearly explain available payment options.

### Requirements

Create a dedicated pricing/packages section.

Include:

* Package name
* Features
* Cost
* Call-to-action button

### Acceptance Criteria

* Pricing is easy to understand.
* Users know exactly what they are paying for.

